ProtoJSON represents `updateMask` as a string containing paths relative to `campaign`, using lower camel case:

```json
{
  "campaign": {
    "name": "campaigns/C7",
    "displayName": "Summer"
  },
  "updateMask": "displayName"
}
```

Predicted stored resource from the original before state:

```json
{
  "name": "campaigns/C7",
  "displayName": "Summer",
  "description": "Approved",
  "spendLimitMicros": "25000000"
}

This starts independently from the original before state:

```json
{
  "campaign": {
    "name": "campaigns/C7",
    "description": ""
  },
  "updateMask": "description"
}
```

Predicted stored resource:

```json
{
  "name": "campaigns/C7",
  "displayName": "Spring",
  "description": "",
  "spendLimitMicros": "25000000"
}
```

Here, selection plus the default value expresses reset. Under this contract, a selected description omitted from the normalized message also resets to `""`. An omitted description outside the mask is preserved.
